\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 + (void)\b setCellClass:\b0 (Class)\i classId\i0  \
\fs14\
\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Configures the NSButton class to use instances of \i classId\i0  for its NSCells. \i classId\i0  should be the \b id\b0  of a subclass of NSButtonCell, obtained by sending the \b class\b0  message to either the NSCell subclass object or to an instance of that subclass. The default NSCell class is NSButtonCell.\
\fs14\
\fs28 If this method isn\'27t overridden by a subclass of NSButton, then when it\'27s sent to that subclass, NSButton and any other subclasses of NSButton will use the new NSCell subclass as well. To safely set an NSCell class for your subclass of NSButton, override this method to store the NSCell class in a static \b id\b0 . Also, override the designated initializer to replace the NSButton subclass instance\'27s NSCell with an instance of the NSCell subclass stored in that static \b id\b0 . See \'aaCreating New NSControls\'ba in the NSControl class specification\'27s class description for more information.\
\fs14\
