\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1  (void)\b getPeriodicDelay:\b0 (float *)\i delay \b \i0 interval:\b0 (float *)\i interval\i0  \
\fs14\
\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Returns by reference the delay and interval periods for a continuous button. \i delay\i0  is the amount of time (in seconds) that the button will pause before starting to periodically send action messages to the target object. \i interval\i0  is the amount of time (also in seconds) between those messages.\
\fs14\
\fs28 Default delay and interval values are taken from a user\'27s defaults (60 seconds maximum for each); if the user hasn\'27t specified default values, \i delay\i0  defaults to 0.4 seconds and \i interval\i0  defaults to 0.075 seconds.\
\fs14\
\pard \s57 \li2804 \fi-1292 \ri1007 \ql \tx2799 \tx3282 \tx3771 \fs28 \f0 \b \fs24 See also:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80\b isContinuous\b0  (NSControl)\
