\fs14\
\fs28 The types available are for the most common button types, which are also accessible in Interface Builder. You can configure different behavior with NSButtonCell\'27s \b setHighlightsBy:\b0  and \b setShowsStateBy:\b0  methods.\
\fs14\
\fs28 \i aType\i0  can be one of eight constants:\
\fs14\
\pard \s62 \li1915 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx6753 \tx9553 \f0 \b \fs28 Button Type\tab Description\
\fs6\
\pard \s60 \li6753 \fi-4838 \ri1007 \ql \tx6753 \tx9525 \f1 \b0 \fs28 NSMomentaryLight\tab While the button is held down it\'27s shown as \'aalit.\'ba This type of button is best for simply triggering actions, as it doesn\'27t show its state; it always displays its normal image or title. This option is called \'aaMomentary Light\'ba in Interface Builder\'27s Button Inspector. This is the default button type.\
\fs14\
\fs28 NSMomentaryPushButton\tab While the button is held down it\'27s shown as \'aalit,\'ba and also \'aapushed in\'ba to the screen if the button is bordered. This type of button is best for simply triggering actions, as it doesn\'27t show its state; it always displays its normal image or title. This option is called \'aaMomentary Push\'ba in Interface Builder\'27s Button Inspector.\
\fs14\
\fs28 NSMomentaryChangeButton\tab \
\fi0 While the button is held down, the alternate image and alternate title are displayed. The normal image or title are displayed when the button isn\'27t pressed. This option is called \'aaMomentary Change\'ba in Interface Builder\'27s Button Inspector.\
\fs14\
\fi-4838 \fs28 NSPushOnPushOffButton\tab The first click both highlights and causes the button to be \'aapushed in\'ba if the button is bordered. A second click returns it to its normal state. This option is called \'aaPush On/Push Off\'ba in Interface Builder\'27s Button Inspector.\
\fs14\
\fs28 NSOnOffButton\tab The first click highlights the button. A second click returns it to the normal (unhighlighted) state. This option is called \'aaOn/Off\'ba in Interface Builder\'27s Button Inspector.\
\fs14\
\fs28 NSToggleButton\tab The first click highlights the button, while a second click returns it to its normal state. Highlighting is performed by changing to the alternate title or image and showing the button as \'aapushed in\'ba if the button is bordered. This option is called \'aaToggle\'ba in Interface Builder\'27s Button Inspector.\
\fs14\
\fs28 NSSwitchButton\tab This is a variant of NSToggleButton that has no border, with the default image set to \'aaNSSwitch,\'ba and the alternate image set to \'aaNSHighlightedSwitch\'ba (these are system bitmaps). This type of button is available as a separate palette item in Interface Builder.\
\fs14\
\fs28 NSRadioButton\tab Like NSSwitchButton, but the default image is set to \'aaNSRadioButton\'ba and the alternate image is set to \'aaNSHighlightedRadioButton\'ba (these are system bitmaps). This type of button is available as a separate palette item in Interface Builder.\
\fs14\
